    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Director--Energy---Engineering_JR103292": {
      "title": "Director, Energy & Engineering",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-31\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Summary:   Manage the HVAC   department   which includes Building Automation, Energy   Center   and HVAC Distribution. Provide a clean,   safe   and comfortable teaching/learning environment for students,   faculty   and staff.   Essential Functions:   25% Manage Superintendents of HVAC Distribution, Building   Automation   and the Energy Center.   20% Develop and perform training for Supervision and skilled trades personnel to meet the changing needs of the department.   Manage the hiring of personnel,   grievances   and disciplinary action. Develop and implement training and compliance   of   all EPA Refrigerant laws and regulations. Develop operating and energy management strategies for campus buildings and systems.   15% Commission new buildings for system/equipment defects, deficiencies and other problems related to construction.   15% Coordinate relevant shops for major equipment and system repairs.   15% Review plans and specs for Capital Planning projects. Develop projects, strategic planning,   write   and   approve   specs for   material,   installation   and electrical.   10% Review mechanical engineers’ estimates to replace or install new boilers, chillers,   RTU's   and air conditioning units. Oversee   contractors and ensure contract compliance.   Additional Position Information: Education:   Requires a relevant   Bachelor's Degree .     Licenses/Certifications/Requirements:   Valid Ohio   Drivers   License     Experience:   Requires a minimum of 3   years experience   in lower/mid management position of a large maintenance organization.     Leadership:   Management of the operation of a unit/major function with activities typically coordinated through administrative personnel above   the level of first-line supervisors or through persons having mid-to-upper-level management or professional responsibility.     Physical Requirements:   Light physical effort required involving stooping and bending; individual has limited discretion about walking, standing, etc.;   occasionally   lifting of   lightweight objects (up to 25 lbs.).     Working Conditions:   Routine discomforts from exposure to moderate levels of heat, cold, moisture/wetness,   noise   and air pollution. May involve   routine/occasional exposure to light chemical substances or hazards (radiation, chemicals, diseases,   heights   and moving parts).     Compensation:   Final salary compensation will be   commensurate   with the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. Application Deadline: Review of applications will begin on September 30, 2026.    Application Instructions:   To apply for this position, applicants must complete the online application and attach a current resume   demonstrating   relevant experience and qualifications that align with the position’s responsibilities and requirements.   FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State 