    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Custodial-Superintendent_JR103070": {
      "title": "Custodial Superintendent",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Summary :   Coordinates and supervises the performance of housekeeping and custodial duties while  maintaining  records of hours worked   by    employees .  Performs various administrative duties, and ensures compliance with departmental contracts, policies, and procedures.   Essential Functions :   40% Supervises employees and inspects buildings to evaluate employee job performance and enforce compliance with contracts,      policies,  and procedures.     20% Performs various administrative duties including  maintaining  personnel records,  developing  and  monitoring  the departments .      budget, preparing reports, managing supply orders, and controlling inventory.     15%  Anticipates  the housekeeping and custodial needs of the University to plan and coordinate daily work activities effectively .       Develops programs and policies to create a safe and clean environment for the campus community.     15% Provides training and instruction to housekeeping and custodial employees while managing employee work schedules and      recording employee hours.     10% Cooperates with other departments, students, and the  general public  to solve problems, communicate information, and      maintain good public relations. Additional Position Information: Education:   Requires high school diploma. Licenses/Certifications/Requirements:   Valid   Driver’s   License .     Regular schedule changes may be necessary —a   minimum of   forty hours   of mandatory overtime   per calendar   year   is   required .    Experience:   Requires a minimum of 1   year   of   experience   in housekeeping/custodial operations and   the   ability to train and supervise employees .     Knowledge of relevant safety practices, inventory control, budgeting, public relations, and   record-keeping   required .    Strong    communication,   and   problem-solving   skills, and the ability to perform general managerial duties required .     General PC knowledge   is   required .    Must be computer literate with   proficiency   and working knowledge of database and reporting tools such as Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook.   Leadership:   Direct supervision and evaluation of work as a first-line supervisor over non-exempt staff including hiring,   terminating ,    disciplining ,   or functional guidance and/or project leadership over exempt staff engaged in activities   regularly .   Physical Requirements:   Light physical effort   is   required involving stooping and bending;   the   individual has limited discretion about walking, standing,   etc.     occasionally   lifting of   lightweight objects (up to 25 lbs.).   Working Conditions:   Occasional minor discomforts from exposure to less-than-optimal temperatures and air   conditions .    May involve   occasional     exposure to dust, fumes, or outside weather conditions, and/or frequent driving of a vehicle (50% or more of the time). Shift Available :   Monday–Friday, 3:00 p.m.-11:30 p.m. Initial training will be conducted on first shift (6:00 a.m.- 2:30 p.m.). Regular shift may change based on departmental needs.   Compensation :   The hourly rate for this position is $ 18.21.     Learn more about benefits at The University of Akron:   https://www.uakron.edu/hr/benefits/   Application Instructions :   In order to   be considered for this position, please   submit   an online application and attach your resume.   Application Instructions: In order to be considered for this position, please complete the online application and attach your resume.   Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience.   Application Deadline: Review of applicants will begin  FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Non-Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Cindy Harm Email: charm@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
