    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Engineering-Technician-Senior--Machinist_JR102750": {
      "title": "Engineering Technician Senior, Machinist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Summary: Provide technical services to support the College's research and teaching efforts including, but not limited to machine instructions, safety training, maintenance of equipment, design, machining, fabrication and recommendation through installation of new equipment.   Provide assistance to faculty and students while promoting compliance with safety regulations. Essential Functions: 40%-60% Perform various design, machining, fabrication and troubleshooting procedures. Provide support in terms of CAD/CAM. Instruct students and faculty in the appropriate use of machinery, electronic instruments and computers hardware/software. 15% Monitor specific environmental, health and safety regulations and coordinate with other units on campus.  Provide support in terms of CAD/CAM and printing operations. 10 - 15% Recommend, maintain, install, troubleshoot and repair technical equipment. 10% Consult with vendors and oversee purchasing activities to properly secure technical items, supplies and equipment for the College. Additional Position Information: Required Qualifications: Education: Requires 18 months of education or training beyond high school. Associates degree preferred. Licenses/Certifications/Requirements: None. Experience: Requires a minimum of 4 years' experience in CAD/CAM, machining and mechanical design.  Strong communication skills required.  Knowledge of CNC hardware and software as well as manual machining equipment is required. Experience in part design and fabrication using mills, lathes, drill press and sheet metal work. Windows, machine tool and die making and troubleshooting of undergraduate laboratory equipment required.  Journeyman machinist certification preferred. Leadership: Responsible for directing and monitoring the work of student and/or temporary workers. Physical Requirements: Moderate physical effort required involving long periods of standing, walking on rough surfaces, bending and/or stooping; periodic lifting of moderately heavy items (over 25 lbs. -- 50 lbs.). Working Conditions: Routine discomforts from exposure to moderate levels of heat, cold, moisture/wetness, noise and air pollution.  May involve routine/occasional exposure to light chemical substances or hazards (radiation, chemicals, diseases, heights and moving parts). Compensation: Compensation starts at $58,000 and is commensurate with experience. Application Deadline: September4, 2026 Application Instructions: To be considered for this position, please complete the online application and attach your resume. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Shawna Harris Email: lharris@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Coordinator--Student-Conduct---Community-Standards_JR103248": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Student Conduct & Community Standards",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 16 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Summary: Support the day-to-day activities and events related to the Office of Student Conduct and Community Standards. Essential Functions: 90% Assist with the facilitation of a comprehensive university-wide student conduct program (academic and non-academic) as it applies to individual students and student organizations. Facilitate student meetings and hearings, conduct investigations, maintain student conduct records, gather data, prepare reports, and assist in the development of policies and procedures. 5% Assist with the development and implementation of educational programs and training events for the campus community educating community members on community standards, and the student conduct process. 5% Perform other duties and responsibilities as assigned by the Director of Student Conduct and Community Standards. Additional Position Information: Education:   Requires a relevant bachelor's degree with master's degree in Higher Education, Counseling, or Law preferred. Licenses/Certifications/Requirements: None Experience: Requires a minimum of 2 years' experience in higher education environment such as student conduct, residence life and housing, or student affairs, or closely related field which includes experience in an investigation/adjudication environment.  Knowledge of due process requirements and federal and state laws impacting student conduct policies and procedures required. Effective oral and written communication skills, excellent interpersonal skills and administrative capabilities required. Ability to coordinate all aspects of student disciplinary action maintain thorough confidential records required.  Prior experience and training in conducting complex investigations including Title IX, Gender-Based Misconduct, Discrimination, and Hazing cases preferred.  Proficient with Maxient and student management software preferred. Application Instructions : In order to be considered for this position, please complete the online application and attach a cover letter and resume. Application Deadline : For best consideration, apply by September 4, 2026 Applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Compensation : The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Shawna Harris Email: lharris@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Manager--Outdoor-Adventure_JR103241": {
      "title": "Manager, Outdoor Adventure",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-19\nPosted: Posted 17 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Summary: Responsible for the leadership, administration, and strategic oversight of the Outdoor Adventure program, including climbing wall operations, trip programming, adventure programming, equipment rentals, special event programming, and risk management. Position supervises student staff, develops engaging and inclusive outdoor recreation experiences, ensures compliance with industry and University safety standards, and manages program resources to promote student engagement, leadership development, and participant well-being. Essential Functions: Staff Supervision: recruit, hire, train, schedule, and evaluate a team of student employees that support outdoor adventure program operations and fosters a customer service-oriented work environment while promoting student staff development and leadership. Rock Wall area supervision: oversee the daily operations of the indoor climbing wall and bouldering arch that ensures a safe, welcoming, and engaging environment. Develop and maintain operating procedures that comply with industry standards and best practices for climbing wall operations. Adventure Programming and Trip Management: design, implement, and evaluate a comprehensive outdoor adventure program including day trips, overnight excursions, clinics, and experiential learning opportunities. Coordinate all logistical aspects of adventure programming including space allocation, transportation, permits, lodging, risk assessments, participant communication, and trip documentation. Equipment Rentals: manage the outdoor equipment rental program, including inventory management, purchasing, maintenance, repair, replacement planning, and lifecycle tracking. Develop rental policies and procedures, pricing structures, and reservation processes via facility management software. Risk Management: develop, implement, and continuously evaluate comprehensive risk management plans for all outdoor adventure programs and facilities. Ensure compliance with university policies, industry standards, and applicable local, state, and federal regulations. Conduct routine inspections of facilities, equipment, and program sites to identify and mitigate potential hazards. Maintain certifications, staff training records, waivers, and operational documentation. Special Event programming: develop and facilitate experiential team building and leadership development programs for university departments, student organizations, summer camp programs and external clients as necessary. Contribute to departmental revenue generating initiatives including birthday party rentals. Licenses/Certifications Required: CPR, First Aid, & AED certified Wilderness First Aid certified or ability to obtain within 3-months of hirs Preferred Certifications: Wilderness First Responder, Climbing Wall Instructor, Single Pitch Instructor Additional Position Information: Education: relevant Bachelor’s Degree Experience: Requires a minimum of 1 year experience in managing and providing instruction in recreational sports programming such as canoeing, kayaking, backpacking, sailing, climbing, etc.   Supervisory experience of staff and/or students, strong oral and written communication skills, and ability to work a non-traditional work week. Computer skills to include Microsoft Office suite of programs and membership/facility management software.   Application Deadline: September 19, 2026 Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience and qualifications. Application Instructions: in order to be considered for this position, please attach the following documents Cover Letter Resume List of 3 Professional References FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Shawna Harris Email: lharris@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Assistant-Professor--Counseling-Psychology_JR103046-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (TT), Counseling Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSubject to Collective Bargaining Agreement Requirements. The Department of Psychology at the University of Akron ( https://www.uakron.edu/psychology ) invites applications for a (tenure-track) Assistant Professor position starting in August 2027. We seek scholars who will lead collaborations among faculty, students, and community partners that address questions of well-being, public safety, and civic engagement.   We are seeking a teacher/scholar who will offer a strong contribution to UA through teaching, research, service, and collaboration. Within the broad focus of Counseling Psychology, we seek a scholar focused on teaching and researching Counseling Psychology content related to social justice, multiculturalism broadly defined, ethics, and clinical practica. This faculty will also assist with the development of a terminal master’s program in Counseling Psychology. It is also important that the successful candidate can effectively teach undergraduate and graduate psychology courses and effectively advise/mentor graduate students in their research activities. Required Qualifications Applicants must have a PhD in Counseling/Clinical Psychology, be licensed or licensed eligible, and teach undergraduate and graduate psychology courses. Preferred Qualifications Applicants should demonstrate a program of research with the potential for external funding.   Application Instructions Applicants should submit a letter of application, curriculum vitae, Teaching Statement, and Research Statement, and three letters of recommendation.  Direct inquiries to John Queener, queener@uakron.edu.   The Psychology Department Within the University of Akron, the Buchtel College of Arts & Sciences, and the Department of Psychology, research, teaching, and service are central values. The successful candidate will join 13 full-time faculty with well-established doctoral programs in Counseling Psychology, I/O Psychology, and Adult Development and Aging. The I/O Psychology graduate program also offers a terminal M.A. degree, and the department offers a baccalaureate major in Psychology. The applicant for the current position will become a core faculty member in the Counseling Psychology Program, along with three other full-time, tenure-track faculty members. The Psychology Department's three established Doctoral programs in I/O Psychology, Counseling Psychology, and Adult Development and Aging have a synergistic relationship for curricula and research collaboration. More information about the psychology department is provided in the link below:  https://www.uakron.edu/psychology/  Additional Position Information: Teaching and Research Expectations: We seek scholars who will lead collaborations among faculty, students, and community partners that address questions of well-being, public safety, and civic engagement. Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience and qualifications.  Application Deadline: September 30th, 2026. FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): American Association of University Professors For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Iron Bones Email: ibones@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Assistant-Professor--TT---Industrial-and-Organizational-Psychology_JR102926-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor (TT), Industrial and Organizational Psychology",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nSubject to Collective Bargaining Agreement Requirements. The Department of Psychology at the University of Akron (https://www.uakron.edu/psychology/ invites applications for a (tenure-track) Assistant Professor position starting in August 2027. Required Qualifications: We seek to assemble a cohort of teacher-scholars who will offer a strong contribution to the excellence of UA through teaching, scholarship, service and collaboration. Specifically, as an urban-research university, we are particularly interested in scholars whose work touches on the pressing needs of cities and urban communities such as health, career outlooks, and employment. In addition, we seek scholars that will lead collaborations among faculty, students and community partners that address questions of well-being, public safety, and civic engagement. Within the broad focus of I/O Psychology, we seek a scholar focused on teaching and researching content that may include recruitment, selection, performance management, team processes, leadership, culture, well-being, organizational effectiveness, and employee success.  In addition, we seek applicants who provide evidence of research activity/publication in high quality, peer-reviewed I/O Psychology and Management journals.  It is also important that the successful candidate can effectively teach undergraduate and graduate psychology courses and effectively advise/mentor graduate students in their research activities.  Finally, we also expect applicants to have completed the requirements for a Ph.D. in I/O Psychology, or related field, by the position start date of August 23, 2027.  Preferred Qualifications: The mission of the Psychology Department is to prepare students to excel in diverse careers in Health, Education, Business, & Research. We do this by equipping them with the scientific and professional knowledge within a broader and evolving socio-cultural, historical, and systemic context. This equipping is necessary to understand, engage, and improve the condition of individuals, groups, organizations, and society through community-engaged teaching, research, and service which is expected of all of our faculty. Additional Position Information: Teaching and Research Expectations: With almost 400 undergraduate majors and graduating up to 100 per year, Psychology is one of the largest academic units in the Buchtel College of Arts and Sciences. This, coupled with 3 PhD programs and a stand alone MA program in I/O, makes for a very busy, engaged, and exciting department. Hence, our new faculty member will be expected to teach at both the undergraduate level and the graduate level in I/O giving them wonderful opportunities, experiences, and an integral role within this very active department which is one of the leading units on campus. Application Instructions:   In order to be considered for this position, please attach the necessary documents CV, Cover Letter. Teaching and Research Statements, Up to 3 sample research manuscripts, and 3 letters of recommendation Compensation: The compensation for this position is commensurate with experience and qualifications.  Questions about the job should be sent to Dr. Paul E. Levy at pelevy@uakron.edu  or 330-972-8369. Application Deadline: September 30th, 2026 FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): American Association of University Professors For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Iron Bones Email: ibones@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
    "https://uakron.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Akron-Ohio/Assistant-Professor-Instruction_JR103002": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor Instruction",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-26\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nThe UA School of Counseling houses Council for Accreditation of Counseling and Related Educational Programs (CACREP) accredited degrees in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and School Counseling, and Commission on Accreditation for Marriage and Family Therapy Education (COAMFTE) accredited degree in Marriage & Family Therapy.  The School of Counseling has as its mission the goal of training students who: Display a respect for human dignity. Exhibit a commitment to fulfillment of their individual potential. Show an understanding of educational and counseling processes with knowledge in their specific field of endeavor. Apply ethical and competent behavior in the use of counseling skills. Acquire and use knowledge of the roles and functions of others working in related fields. Possess and display maturity in self-development. Understand issues and trends of a multicultural and diverse society. Additional Position Information: REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: (1) Earned doctorate degree in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program. ABD will be considered but a doctorate degree must be conferred prior to the position start date (including follow-up confirmation from the dissertation chairperson stating that the dissertation defense has been scheduled may be required); (2) Experience working with counseling graduate students in instruction, clinical supervision, and/or scholarly activities; (3) Licensed or license eligible as a Licensed Professional Counselor or Licensed Professional Clinical Counselor in the State of Ohio PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: 1) Involvement in or affiliation with professional counseling organizations (e.g., ACA, ACES, state-level associations and/or subdivisions); (2) Successful use of technology in in-person, hybrid, and online instruction and/or clinical supervision; (3) A successful record of scholarly activities (publications, presentations, and/or grant writing) To apply for this position, you must (a) complete the online application and (b) attach the necessary documents including CV, Cover Letter, Teaching Philosophy, Graduate Transcripts, and Contact Information of 3 Professional References. Application Deadline: September 24, 2026 FLSA Status (exempt/nonexempt): United States of America (Exempt) Union Affiliation (if applicable): American Association of University Professors For assistance with your application or attachments, please contact the Human Resources representative listed: Danielle Ester (Private) Email: dester@uakron.edu ________________________________________________________________________ Background Check Statement The University of Akron is committed to providing a safe environment for all students and employees.  The University endeavors to protect the health, welfare and safety of all students, employees and visitors on our campus.  As such, all offers of employment with The University of Akron are contingent upon verification of credentials, and satisfactory completion of a criminal background check. Some positions may require additional credit investigation and a pre-employment driving record search.  Non-Discrimination Statement The University of Akron is an Equal Education and Employment Institution. View our Non-Discrimination Statement for more information. Equal Opportunity Employer, including disability/veterans. State of Residence Statement It is the expectation of the University of Akron that all work performed as an employee of the University will be performed in Ohio."
    },
